      "text": "To find the average value of the numbers \\(0\\), \\(2z\\), \\(4z\\), \\(8z\\), and \\(16z\\), we start by calculating the sum of these numbers. The sum is:\n\n\\[\n0 + 2z + 4z + 8z + 16z\n\\]\n\nWe can combine the like terms:\n\n\\[\n0 + 2z + 4z + 8z + 16z = (0 + 2 + 4 + 8 + 16)z = 30z\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to find the average value by dividing the sum by the number of terms. There are 5 terms, so we divide \\(30z\\) by 5:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{30z}{5} = 6z\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the average value of \\(0\\), \\(2z\\), \\(4z\\), \\(8z\\), and \\(16z\\) is \\(\\boxed{6z}\\).",
