      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "First, we find the sum of these five quantities:\n\\begin{align*}\n\\text{Sum} &= 0 + 2z + 4z + 8z + 16z \\\\\n&= (0 + 2z) + (4z + 8z) + 16z \\\\\n&= 2z + 12z + 16z \\\\\n&= (2 + 12 + 16)z \\\\\n&= 30z.\n\\end{align*}\n\nNext, we find the average by dividing the sum by the number of terms. There are 5 terms in total, so:\n\\begin{align*}\n\\text{Average} &= \\frac{\\text{Sum}}{\\text{Number of terms}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{30z}{5} \\\\\n&= \\boxed{6z}.\n\\end{align*}\n\nTherefore, the average value of $0$, $2z$, $4z$, $8z$, and $16z$ is $\\boxed{6z}$.",
